{"type":"message","id":"89d1c3ad","parentId":"cf7cbeab","timestamp":"2026-04-27T06:39:01.748Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Doctor Agent assessment**\nHere is the diagnostic support returned by the Doctor Agent based on your records, symptoms, and HRV upload.\n\n**Diagnostic interpretation**\nThe overall pattern is most consistent with a **stress-related health burden** that may be affecting mood, sleep, concentration, and physical symptoms together. The combination of **poor sleep, headaches, fatigue, irritability, and trouble concentrating**, together with your prior rise in **PHQ-9 score, blood pressure, resting heart rate, cortisol, and stress index**, supports a picture of worsening stress physiology, with depressive symptoms still remaining a meaningful part of the picture.\n\n**Likely explanations**\nThe most likely explanation is **ongoing stress-system activation over time**, with possible **HPA-axis dysregulation**, which is broadly compatible with the FKBP5-related background in your genomics summary. Poor sleep may also be reinforcing the daytime fatigue, irritability, headaches, and concentration problems. The COMT finding may fit a higher-arousal stress response profile, but it does not by itself diagnose the cause of symptoms.\n\n**Important uncertainties**\nThese findings do not prove that stress is the only cause of your symptoms. The genomic information suggests **susceptibility, not certainty**, and it cannot confirm a diagnosis on its own. Your current symptoms could reflect overlapping contributors, including mood-related symptoms, sleep disruption, or other non-genetic factors not fully captured in the information provided. Your dermatology and genomic background, including melanoma and UV-sensitivity risk, remains relevant to your overall health history, but it does not appear to be the main active issue here unless you are also having skin-related symptoms.\n\n**What the HRV upload adds**\nThe uploaded pulse series appears to show a heart rate mostly in the **mid-50s** with **mild beat-to-beat variation** during that short evening window. That gives only a limited snapshot and does not show obvious large swings in pulse during the recording period. However, because there were **no formal HRV-derived metrics** and this was only a **short single time window**, it does not meaningfully confirm or rule out autonomic dysregulation, chronic stress burden, or depression-related physiology.\n\n**Next step**\nBecause stress and depression-related concerns are present here, you can upload an **audio file** and I will run the **voice depression detection pipeline** to add another preliminary signal to the current picture.","textSignature":"{\"v\":1,\"id\":\"msg_04ec2a99e9130d0b0169ef047ce10c81918651aedcf0b589cc\",\"phase\":\"final_answer\"}"}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-5.4","usage":{"input":646,"output":488,"cacheRead":28672,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":29806,"cost":{"input":0.0016150000000000001,"output":0.00732,"cacheRead":0.007168,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.016103}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1777271931873,"responseId":"resp_04ec2a99e9130d0b0169ef047c317c819199e10064c83f4f82"}}
