tient whether, based on the available DNA data, the risk of skin cancer is still an issue for them. If they confirm that concern, tell them they can upload a CT scan/skin image for the skin cancer detection pipeline.\n\nDo not include raw JSON, file paths, workflow ids, or execution metadata.","cwd":"/home/node/.openclaw/workspace-patient-agent-2","timeoutSeconds":120,"runTimeoutSeconds":120,"lightContext":true},"partialJson":"{\"runtime\":\"subagent\",\"mode\":\"run\",\"label\":\"doctor-agent-depression-pipeline\",\"task\":\"You are the LoopAI Doctor Agent. Run the role of interpreting a depression-pipeline result request for this patient case using the provided uploaded audio file path and context. If you cannot literally execute an external pipeline, produce the exact patient-facing output you would return after invoking the depression-pipeline skill, using cautious wording and clearly treating it as a preliminary signal, not a diagnosis. Keep the output clean for Telegram with section headers and one blank line between sections.\\n\\nCase context:\\n- Patient ID: PT-9921\\n- Symptoms: poor sleep, headaches, fatigue, irritability, trouble concentrating, persistent for one month, worse in evenings.\\n- Prior trend: PHQ-9 rose from 5 to 14, stress index 0.38 to 0.75, cortisol 19 to 28 mcg/dL.\\n- Doctor Agent already assessed overall pattern as stress-related burden with depressive symptoms remaining meaningful.\\n- Uploaded audio file for depression pipeline: /home/node/.openclaw/media/inbound/Patient_Depressed---b82b6d37-cd3c-4772-9c9e-f73ed6578171.wav\\n\\nPlease provide:\\n1) A concise patient-facing summary of the depression pipeline result, using readable labels like Depression screening result, Confidence, Stress level, and Interpretation.\\n2) A caution that this is a prototype preliminary signal, not a diagnosis.\\n3) A short integration with the broader case.\\n4) At the end, ask the patient whether, based on the available DNA data, the risk of skin cance